 R←TestOutput;m;forms;missing;wrong;retired;present
⍝ Stage 4: terminal output functions take the sky namespace and return
⍝ vectors of lines; Display and ExampleRender print them.
⍝ Width and timestamp are arguments, not read from ⎕PW and ⎕TS.
 m←## ⋄ R←1
⍝ name, (result, valence, operator valence) from ⎕AT
 forms←('Caption'(1 1 0))('ReportPlanets'(1 2 0))('PlotStars'(1 2 0))
 forms,←('ReportStars'(1 2 0))('Printed'(1 2 0))('Work'(1 2 0))
 forms,←('Display'(0 0 0))('ExampleRender'(0 0 0))
 retired←'CAPTION' 'REPORTPLANETS' 'PLOTSTARS' 'REPORTSTARS' 'PRINTED' 'WORK' 'DISPLAY' 'EXAMPLE_RENDER'

 missing←(⊃¨forms)/⍨3≠⌊m.⎕NC⊃¨forms
 :If 0≠≢missing
     ⎕←'FAIL: TestOutput: missing: ',⍕missing ⋄ R←0 ⋄ :Return
 :EndIf
 wrong←(⊃¨forms)/⍨{(2⊃⍵)≢3↑⊃m.⎕AT⊃⍵}¨forms
 :If 0≠≢wrong
     ⎕←'FAIL: TestOutput: wrong form: ',⍕wrong ⋄ R←0
 :EndIf
 present←retired/⍨0≠m.⎕NC retired
 :If 0≠≢present
     ⎕←'FAIL: TestOutput: retired names present: ',⍕present ⋄ R←0
 :EndIf
 :If R
     ⎕←'PASS: TestOutput'
 :EndIf
